Everything under this directory comes from the 5th Red List of Japan
(環境省 第５次レッドリスト), published by the Ministry of the Environment,
Japan, Nature Conservation Bureau, on the Ikimono Log page
https://ikilog.biodic.go.jp/Rdb/booklist .

That page, read on 2026-10-03 and checked again when the files were fetched
on 2026-10-04 (UTC), says in its section 「第５次レッドリストについて（令和7年～）」,
directly above the table of the eight CSV files:

  なお、以下のレッドリスト（CSV版）は、クリエイティブ・コモンズ 表示 4.0
  国際ライセンス（CC BY 4.0）の下で公表されています。

("The following Red Lists (CSV versions) are published under CC BY 4.0.")
The page gives no example of how to credit the source. Credit it, for
example, as:

  出典：環境省 第５次レッドリスト（いきものログ https://ikilog.biodic.go.jp/Rdb/booklist）、CC BY 4.0
  Source: Ministry of the Environment, Japan, 5th Red List (Ikimono Log), CC BY 4.0

The files under raw/5th/ are the Ministry's CSVs, byte for byte;
raw/5th/MANIFEST.json records their URLs, sizes, sha256 and Last-Modified.

The Parquet under parquet/5th/ was made from those CSVs by
yuiseki/env-redlist-jp, not by the Ministry:

  - decoded from cp932 or UTF-8 with a BOM, as each file is, into UTF-8
  - the three header rows of the 2026 files (birds, reptiles, amphibians)
    flattened into one name per column, "<row 2>_<row 3>", or "<row 3>"
    where row 2 is empty; the original rows are kept in each file's
    key-value metadata (source_header_rows) and in README.md
  - the habitat, region and threat columns of the 2026 files, which hold
    0 or 1, typed as INTEGER; every other column is the text of the CSV
  - no value was changed: categories, brackets, numerals, dashes and
    spaces are as the Ministry wrote them

The earlier editions on the same page (1991 to Red List 2020, the marine
Red List) are not included; the page states no licence for them.

The code that fetches, checks and converts is in the repository this dataset
was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/env-redlist-jp) and does not
apply here.
